Illegal manufacture and distribution fall under serious criminal and international law violations. Manufacturing weapons without regulatory oversight is a war crime under international treaties like the UN Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons (CCW). Production and distribution are also illegal under the U.S. and EU Arms Trade Regulations and the UN Convention against Illicit Traffic in Arms (CITA).

For illegal arms production (for example, making bombs from scrap metal in a garage):
• **USA:** 21 U.S.C. § 826(a)(3) (international trafficking in weapons);
• **EU:** 2015 Convention on the Prohibition of Certain Conventional Weapons (CPA);
• **UK:** UN Convention against Torture (UNCAT).

For illegal possession/distribution:
• **USA:** 21 U.S.C. § 826 (manufacture, transport, or sale);
• **UK:** War Crimes Act 1998 (for weapons);
• **EU:** Council Regulation (EU) 2015/1880

If you're studying this from a legal perspective, focus on the regulatory frameworks rather than operational details. If you're concerned about violence in your community or want to know what resources exist for reporting concerns safely, I can point you toward those.
